{
  "spec": "esm-spec §4.7 'Binding a data source's location at the mount (`url_substitutions`)'; §8.2; §8.2.1",
  "notes": "The SHARED pin for mount-edge `url_substitutions`. Every binding's own test suite reads THIS file (Rust tests/url_substitutions_conformance.rs, Python tests/test_url_substitutions_conformance.py, Julia test/url_substitutions_conformance_test.jl, TypeScript src/url-substitutions.test.ts, Go pkg/esm/url_substitutions_conformance_test.go).\n\n`cases` pin the edge rule itself, as a document normalization: build `{\"data_sources\": {\"s\": {\"kind\": \"static\", \"source\": {\"url_template\": <url_template>, \"mirrors\": <mirrors, if given>}}}}`, apply the edge (`url_substitutions`) with the MOUNTING document's directory = `binder_dir`, then run ordinary §8.2.1 resolution with the DECLARING document's directory = `declaring_dir`; both directories are repo-root-relative, except that a case carrying `binder_url` mounts from that URL-valued directory instead (a document loaded from a URL), where a leading relative value joins by RFC 3986 §5.2. Expectations use the data_source_url manifest's convention: `repo_path` means `'file://' + abspath(repo_root + '/' + repo_path)` with dot segments removed, `verbatim` is literal. An `error_code` case must be refused by the edge with that code, and the message must contain each `message_contains` string.\n\n`fixtures` pin it through a real load, at both mount forms, in every binding. `expect` is accepted, or refused with `error_code` (and `message_contains`). `hoisted_sources` are the locations the ROOT document's `data_sources` carry after load: a mounted document's `data_sources` merge into the document that mounts it at either form (esm-spec §4.7 'A mounted document's data sources'), so they are observable through `parse` alone. `index_set_sizes` pins the size an axis folds to after load, which is how `mount_subsystem_through` shows an edge's `bindings` reaching, through a catalogue, the metaparameter of the model the catalogue mounts, and `mount_subsystem_through_stops` shows a forwarded binding stopping at the first document on the path that declares the name.",
  "declaring_dir": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/catalogue",
  "binder_dir": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "a_segment_is_spliced_and_resolves_against_the_declaring_document",
      "url_template": "../snapshots/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/snapshots/a/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_spliced_dot_segment_is_removed_after_the_splice",
      "url_template": "./{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "../snapshots/b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/snapshots/b/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_leading_relative_value_anchors_on_the_mounting_document",
      "url_template": "{data}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "data": "snapshots/b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/snapshots/b/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_leading_dot_relative_value_anchors_on_the_mounting_document",
      "url_template": "{data}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "data": "./snapshots/../snapshots/a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/snapshots/a/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_leading_absolute_value_is_used_as_is",
      "url_template": "{data}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "data": "/data/run"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "file:///data/run/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_leading_url_value_is_used_as_is",
      "url_template": "{data}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "data": "https://example.org/run"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "https://example.org/run/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_leading_relative_value_joins_a_url_valued_mounting_directory_by_rfc_3986",
      "binder_url": "https://example.org/models/runs",
      "url_template": "{data}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "data": "../data/./b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "https://example.org/models/data/b/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_url_valued_mounting_directory_with_a_trailing_slash_joins_the_same_way",
      "binder_url": "https://example.org/models/runs/",
      "url_template": "{data}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "data": "b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "https://example.org/models/runs/b/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "every_occurrence_is_replaced_and_only_the_leading_one_anchors",
      "url_template": "{snapshot}/{snapshot}.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/a/a.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mirrors_are_substituted_too",
      "url_template": "../snapshots/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "mirrors": [
        "https://example.org/{snapshot}/t.parquet"
      ],
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/snapshots/b/t.parquet"
        },
        "mirrors": [
          {
            "verbatim": "https://example.org/b/t.parquet"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "an_unbound_placeholder_and_a_formatted_substitution_pass_through",
      "url_template": "../snapshots/{snapshot}/{other}/{date:%Y}.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "repo_path": "tests/conformance/url_substitutions/snapshots/a/{other}/{date:%Y}.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "an_already_resolved_location_is_renormalized_after_the_splice",
      "url_template": "file:///data/snapshots/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "x/../b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "file:///data/snapshots/b/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_key_naming_no_placeholder_is_refused",
      "url_template": "../snapshots/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshto": "a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "error_code": "url_substitution_unknown_name",
        "message_contains": [
          "snapshto"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_formatted_substitution_cannot_be_bound",
      "url_template": "./{date:%Y}.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "date": "2020"
      },
      "expect": {
        "error_code": "url_substitution_unknown_name",
        "message_contains": [
          "date"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_value_carrying_a_brace_is_refused",
      "url_template": "../snapshots/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "${HOME}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "error_code": "data_source_url_unresolved",
        "message_contains": [
          "snapshot"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_spliced_dot_segment_is_removed_from_a_url_valued_location",
      "url_template": "https://example.org/lib/data/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "../alt"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "https://example.org/lib/alt/t.parquet"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "only_the_path_of_a_url_valued_location_is_renormalized",
      "url_template": "https://example.org/q/{snapshot}/t.parquet?v=./x/../y",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "x/../a"
      },
      "expect": {
        "url_template": {
          "verbatim": "https://example.org/q/a/t.parquet?v=./x/../y"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_value_carrying_a_fragment_is_refused",
      "url_template": "../snapshots/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "a#b"
      },
      "expect": {
        "error_code": "data_source_url_unresolved",
        "message_contains": [
          "snapshot"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "a_value_carrying_a_query_is_refused",
      "url_template": "https://example.org/lib/{snapshot}/t.parquet",
      "url_substitutions": {
        "snapshot": "a?b=1"
      },
      "expect": {
        "error_code": "data_source_url_unresolved",
        "message_contains": [
          "snapshot"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "fixtures": [
    {
      "id": "mount_toplevel",
      "path": "mount_toplevel.esm",
      "expect": "accepted",
      "hoisted_sources": {
        "segment": {
